@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] audi-authority-boundary
Audi MUST implement its own authoritative DNS and SSH gateway. Marshall Ash
resources remain durable identity, access and placement authority. Audi MUST NOT
access Marshall's database or grant access from DNS answers alone.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] audi-local-placement-only
Guest streams MUST bind the current placement and execution epoch through
Lilly's restricted connector at the execution host. A one-hop relay MAY use only
operator-configured authenticated fleet peers and a single-use capability bound
to the exact inner lease, origin, destination and peer address. Expired authority
MUST terminate existing streams as well as reject new streams. Neither wake
receipts nor relay routing MAY grant arbitrary TCP or bypass local execution checks.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] audi-bounded-untrusted-input
Network decoders MUST bound packet sizes, recursion, buffers and concurrency.
Peer strings MUST NOT create atoms. Diagnostics MUST NOT contain raw packets,
URLs, headers, credentials, HTTP bodies or SSH payloads.
